A||||9||My7Fieros||Check out tweeter location! PICS...||||14||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||12-16-2000||12:34 AM||||What do you think about this? I just installed two new tweeters in the roof of my 86 Gt. What I did was, after installing a new headliner (which I did on my own for the jillionth time..done it on every one of my Fieros..cheap and easy!), I removed the sun visors..I then bought two tweeters and installed them where the sun visors used to be. They screw in, and one of the holes where the sun visors screw in lined up perfectly! No drilling required! The only drawback is that you loose your visors..but this is my winter car and the sun never shows itself here in the winter lol.<BR>The speakers are Jensen brand, and I bought them at Wallyworld for 29 bucks! The sound GREAT, and as you can see, the even pivot...whadda ya think?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/speaker_4.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tweeter2.jpg"> <P>||||reg||14
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||12-16-2000||01:23 AM||||Hey, I think they look sweet!  Nice work.<P>James||||reg||1
Z||000002||Stoic||12-16-2000||08:22 AM||||Very nice!!  I may just have to do that myself.||||reg||6
Z||000003||overlord||12-16-2000||08:31 AM||||OMG SWEET MERCIFULL CRAP!!......o wait..its just speakers.<BR>Seriouylsy those look good, and now i know where im gonna put my tweeters.  I dont think ive ever used my sunvisor anyways. I wuld never of thought of doing that. Whenver i start thinking, it involves drills. -).<P>Looks good man.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||12-16-2000||10:13 AM||||Those look nice. I am in the process of installing tweeters on the back sail panel area. Took me a few days to match the color. Once they are painted and mounted I'll take some pic's.<BR>Did those come with their own crossover or did you have to provide your own?||||reg||14
