Z||000007||Sndfr||12-16-2000||02:34 PM||||That's awesome, I love it, very creative, we got MacGuyver over here.  But...<P>You ruined it by having that Ford Mudstain in the background!  <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/icw/003.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/scorchio/sevil.gif">  <B>Matthew "Whyt Nyte" D.</B>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/scorchio/sgrin.gif">       <BR><B><I>84 SE</B>- automatic, rare Fender Delete option<BR>"Fender gap?  What fender gap?"</I><BR><B>(future owner of a 60's-70's Chevy muscle car)</B><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/ut2/redcap.gif">                <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/ut1/mgwhore.gif"> ||||reg||13
Z||000008||Philphine||12-16-2000||03:32 PM||||you don't have to take out the visors. i did my first few cars like that and put them in the visor it's self. even gives you a bit of aimability by adjusting the visor. you can even put the visors to the side like you're blocking out the sun in the side windows and kind of get a headphone thing goin'. i stopped doing it because i was going for that equal pathlenth idea and putting them there put the drivers side tweeter too close to my ear. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||My7Fieros||12-16-2000||10:17 PM||||I was at Wal Mart and saw the speakers..for 29 bucks I figured I had nothing to loose! I was overwhelmed at how much more they add to the overall sound!<BR><B> OREIF </B>: I didnt use crossovers..I simply spiced them into the front speakers. The wires run down under the pillar covers..I had to remove them anyway when redoing the headliner. You cant see them at all!<P><B>Stoic</B>: Go for it! Its an easy and inexpensive mod and well worth it.<P><B>Sndfr</B>: LOL..that Mustang in the 1st pic is my roommates...he owns Fieros also though, so dont worry!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><B>Philphine</B> I tried to keep my visors also, but there was no way they were goin in with the speakers there..oh well, no biggie! <p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 12-16-2000).]||||reg||14
